            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Pandoc"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "metadata": {
                  "rel": "noopener",
                  "window": "_blank"
                },
                "target": "https://pandoc.org"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is a Swiss army knife for converting one markup format to another. It does an admirable job converting simple docx files to AsciiDoc."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Generally, we don’t like to recommend pandoc because it doesn’t create AsciiDoc the way we prefer. However, in this case, it’s a good choice."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To perform the conversion from MS Word docx to AsciiDoc, you need to perform the following command:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ pandoc -f docx -t asciidoctor --wrap=none --atx-headers \\\n  --extract-media=extracted-media -o output.adoc"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pandoc < 2.11.2"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ pandoc input.docx -f docx -t asciidoc --wrap=none --markdown-headings=atx \\\n  --extract-media=extracted-media -o output.adoc"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pandoc (2.11.2 or newer)"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you use docker you can also use the latest version of pandoc with docker without installing it:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "pandoc (2.11.2 or newer) and docker"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "context": "literal",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "$ docker run --rm --volume \"$PWD:/data\" --user `id -u`:`id -g` pandoc/core input.docx -f docx \\\n  -t asciidoc --wrap=none --markdown-headings=atx --extract-media=extracted-media -o output.adoc"
              }
            ],
            "language": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Then, edit the output file to tidy it up."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
